{
  "id": "ss.relic.dung-ripe",
  "name": "Ripe ball",
  "description": "The find that stops the ball needing a rock: packed past what it can hold, it goes off where it stands. Drawn as the ball from above, swollen out of round, with a bright seam opened from the top to the middle of it and gas standing out of the seam in three rising motes — the seam pale and hot along its lip and dark in the gap, so it reads as something opening under pressure rather than as a crack in a stone. It stays off `ss.relic.dung` by being the same ball in the opposite condition: that one is a ball with something heavy sealed inside it, this one is a ball that cannot stay shut.",
